@startuml
title LegacyVault Demo Billing and In-App Notifications
autonumber

actor Visitor
actor "Vault Owner" as Owner
participant "Pricing / Billing UI" as UI
participant "Plans / Billing API" as API
participant "BillingService" as Service
database "MySQL" as DB
participant "MockPaymentGateway" as Gateway
participant "NotificationService" as Notifications

Visitor -> UI: Open pricing page
UI -> API: GET /api/v1/plans
API -> Service: Read fixed plan catalog
Service --> API: Free, Essentials, Plus
API --> UI: Prices and limits

Owner -> UI: Add a payment method using demo token
UI -> API: POST /api/v1/billing/payment-methods
note right of UI
Only a provider token and masked card metadata
are sent. Never send PAN or CVV to this API.
end note
API -> Service: Validate Vault Owner and expiry
Service -> DB: Store token + masked card metadata
DB --> Service: Saved payment method
Service --> UI: Masked payment method response

Owner -> UI: Choose plan, billing cycle, and accept recurring terms
UI -> API: POST /api/v1/billing/checkout
API -> Service: Resolve price from server catalog
Service -> DB: Load owner's saved method
DB --> Service: Provider token + masked details
Service -> Gateway: Charge demo token and server amount
alt Demo payment approved
  Gateway --> Service: Approved + mock reference
  Service -> DB: Save successful transaction
  Service -> DB: Activate account plan for one month/year, auto-renew on
  Service -> Notifications: Create payment-success notice
  Notifications -> DB: Save notice for owner
  Service --> API: SUCCEEDED + transaction + subscription
else Demo token ends with _declined
  Gateway --> Service: Declined
  Service -> DB: Save failed transaction
  Service -> Notifications: Create payment-failure notice
  Notifications -> DB: Save notice for owner
  Service --> API: FAILED + transaction + unchanged subscription
end
API --> UI: Display success or failure result

== Period end ==
BillingRenewalScheduler -> Service: Scan subscriptions due for renewal
Service -> DB: Load due ACTIVE subscriptions
DB --> Service: Due subscriptions + default payment methods
Service -> Gateway: Charge mock token for server-calculated renewal amount
alt Renewal approved
  Gateway --> Service: Approved + mock reference
  Service -> DB: Record transaction and extend period
  Service -> Notifications: Create renewal-success notice
else Renewal declined or method unavailable
  Gateway --> Service: Declined
  Service -> DB: Record failed transaction and set PAST_DUE (7 days)
  Service -> Notifications: Create renewal-failure notice
  Owner -> UI: Replace default method and retry within grace period
  UI -> API: POST /api/v1/billing/subscription/retry-payment
  API -> Service: Retry with current default method
end
Owner -> UI: Toggle automatic renewal on or off
UI -> API: PUT /api/v1/billing/subscription/auto-renew {autoRenew}
API -> Service: Update the paid subscription renewal setting
Service -> DB: Save auto_renew; do not charge immediately

Owner -> UI: Open notification inbox
UI -> API: GET /api/v1/notifications
API -> Notifications: List notices for authenticated user only
Notifications -> DB: Query user's notices
DB --> Notifications: Notice list + unread count
Notifications --> API: Paginated response
API --> UI: Display inbox
Owner -> UI: Mark all notifications as read
UI -> API: POST /api/v1/notifications/mark-all-read
API -> Notifications: Update only current user's records
Notifications -> DB: Persist read timestamp

note over Gateway,DB
This is a demo adapter only. No real payment is made.
end note
@enduml
